## Verify Your Installation

Follow the
[installation directions](https://github.com/pettarin/volumito/blob/main/README.md#installation)
in the main
[README](https://github.com/pettarin/volumito/blob/main/README.md)
to install `volumito`.

If the installation went well, you should be able to run the `version` command,
printing the version of the `volumito` tool itself:

```bash lucio command=execute
volumito version
```

Check that you can connect to the Volumio host by issuing the `info` command:

```bash lucio command=execute
volumito --host volumio.local info
```

where `volumio.local` is the local name of the Volumio host.
You can also use its IP address, if you know it.
Clearly you can also use the shorthand `-H`
instead of the full option name `--host`.

If your Volumio host runs on ports different than the default ones,
you might need to add:

- `-M / --mpd-port INTEGER` (default: `6600`)
- `-P / --rest-api-port INTEGER` (default: `3000`)
- `-W / --websocket-port INTEGER` (default: `3000`)
- `--scheme [http|https]` (default: `http`).

> [!NOTE]
> The MPD port is `6600` in Volumio >= 4, and `6599` in Volumio < 4.

For example, to connect to a Volumio 3 instance at local IP address `192.168.1.3`
whose REST API is proxied to port 4567:

```bash
volumito -H 192.168.1.3 -M 6599 -P 4567 ...
```

By default, the commands talk to the Volumio host through its REST API, synchronously.
The `-C / --api-client` option selects another of the clients of the `volumito` library:
`asynchronous_rest` (requiring the `async` extra),
`synchronous_websocket`, or `asynchronous_websocket` (both requiring the `websocket` extra).
The short forms `sync_rest` or `sr`, `async_rest` or `ar`, `sync_websocket` or `sw`,
and `async_websocket` or `aw` are accepted too.
For example, to issue the `info` command over the WebSocket API:

```bash
volumito -C synchronous_websocket info
volumito -C sw info
```

The WebSocket API offers neither the `story` nor the `notification` commands:
with a WebSocket client selected, they fail,
unless the `--allow-fallback-to-rest-api` option lets them use a REST API client.

